            <description><![CDATA[<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,system-ui;margin:0;padding:0;color:#111}h2{font-size:15px;margin:0 0 8px}h3{font-size:13px;margin:12px 0 4px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin-bottom:6px}code{font:11px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo;background:rgba(127,127,127,.15);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#eee}}</style><h2>Version 1.0.3</h2><ul><li>The ODO name in the popover and Settings now matches the logo on odo.bymayo.co.uk</li><li>A shorter behind-pace reminder: how far behind you are, and one weekly figure to aim for</li><li>If Strava turns Odo away because its API now needs a Strava subscription, Odo says so and links to Strava&#x27;s subscribe page instead of showing &quot;Forbidden&quot;. The setup guide mentions it up front</li></ul>]]></description>
